 "layer_cap": "M5",
 "structural_change": "STW-S81e-FP 10-23 (COORD tile review, S81.STA.PAR.3): F2 = F band with SEAM PIN FLOPS.  l1fb_f gate (18:41) classified: (a) s0a[42] -> fold compare (14 levels, ~570 ps cells, < 60 ps wire) -> m1b -615 ps SS = LOGIC DEPTH behind 1,312+51 unregistered seam pins (the A bands' sort / adder flops feed the fold through the abutted seam); (b) ctl_lo[4] -153 ps = WIRE (one s_bn flop drives an S AND an N pin).  RTL dsdv_gunit_l1f_bf2: every seam input lands in a face flop (+1 edge on the merge path, booked MU.S81.CAL), ctl_hi gets its own kept flop copy.  Floorplan: the 18:41 placement used x < 324 only (pd 0.4 packs 15.8k um2 into 55% of the core) and cut x=108 carried 6,368 nets over 172.8 um (~5.5k usable horizontal M2+M4 tracks: bits/tracks 1.16); fb/fc (pd 0.22, full spread, 172.8) still overflowed M4 15.9k at the fold (x~250).  F2 spreads the fold by its face flops along both seams (x 21.6..410.4) and sizes the height from the tracks: 216 um (+25% horizontal tracks; l1f stack 518.4).  Clock W-face middle, default CTS tree.",
 "why_floorplan": "middle row band (432 wide = the CLOSED A bands): W face = stack inputs (W input flops at the face), SC store + write decode + beat read in the W half, fold / m1 / cx8_2 spread along the seam pin flops (S = A_lo sort, N = A_hi sort, x 21.6..410.4), gather + the 246-b output stage under the E pins; per-face ctl flops.",
